# Local overrides. The deployed site does not need this file — netlify.toml sets
# VITE_WAITLIST_FORM, and the API key is a Netlify secret, never a repo file.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The domain. Unset, the app calls itself getniyyah.netlify.app — a subdomain
# of Netlify's domain, not ours, baked into every link ever sent to another
# person and into every share image. The day we own a domain, set this in
# Netlify and redeploy; it is read by src/lib/site.ts and by vite.config.ts,
# which writes it into the social-card tags. Keep the Netlify subdomain alive
# afterwards so links already in people's messages keep working.
# See docs/CONTROL.md.
# VITE_SITE_HOST=niyyah.app

# Where a signup reaches a human when the form is not configured. The default,
# salaam@niyyah.app, is only real if that domain is owned and receiving mail —
# if it bounces, someone who tried to join is lost silently.
# VITE_CONTACT_EMAIL=salaam@niyyah.app

# Netlify Forms: the form name signups are posted to. Set in netlify.toml for
# the deploy; set it here only if you're pointing a local build at Netlify.
# VITE_WAITLIST_FORM=niyyah-waitlist

# Or any endpoint that accepts a JSON POST of { contact, code, scene, gender, hardestPart, at }
# — Airtable, a Google Apps Script, a Supabase function, your own /api route.
# Used only when VITE_WAITLIST_FORM is unset.
VITE_WAITLIST_URL=

# With neither set the app will NOT pretend anyone joined: the signup card falls
# back to a mailto so nothing is silently lost.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is deliberately NOT listed here. It belongs only in Netlify's
# environment (secret scope), because it is read by netlify/functions/guide.ts
# on the server and must never reach the browser bundle or the repository.
#
# Setting it switches the live Guide on, which means members' answers start
# leaving their device — so the Trust screen's privacy copy must be rewritten in
# the same change. See the README.
#
# FOUNDER_KEY is not listed here either. It gates the readouts — the ladder, the
# full tally on the door, the couple tally, the guide's health check — behind
# `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Unset means open, so local runs and tests need
# nothing. Set it in Netlify's environment (secret scope is fine for Node
# functions) and confirm a bare GET on /progress returns 401. See the README.
